r years. An acquirer paying on an EBITDA multiple would struggle to justify more than £5.2m for the equity, as they are essentially buying a melting ice cube. The gap between the £11.4m asset value and the £5.2m earnings value suggests the business is worth more in a liquidation or 'harvest' scenario than as a strategic acquisition, unless the buyer can immediately plug the £19m revenue stream into a growth engine. Any offer should be heavily weighted toward an earn-out or contingent on the retention of the top 5 customers who hold 62% of the company's value."},"deal_structure":{"expert":"deal_structure","company_name":"Latest company Ltd","analysis_date":"2024-05-22","score":45,"confidence":"high","structures":[{"name":"Conservative Approach","strategy":"Protect capital by anchoring the price to the earnings-based valuation (£5.2m) rather than the asset value, with heavy contingency on revenue stabilization.","risk_to_buyer":"low","suitable_when":"The buyer is highly concerned about the 10% annual revenue decline and the 62% customer concentration risk.","consideration":{"total_headline":5222888,"upfront_cash":2089155,"upfront_percent":40,"deferred":1044578,"earnout_maximum":2089155,"earnout_metric":"Revenue Stabilization & Customer Retention","earnout_period_months":24,"earnout_rationale":"Addresses 'Revenue decline' (Valuation/Risk Experts) and 'Customer concentration' (Risk Expert). Earnout is split: 50% on maintaining revenue above £16m floor and 50% on retention of the top 5 named customers.","retention_escrow":522289},"key_conditions":["Retention of top 5 customers representing 62% of revenue","Minimum Net Working Capital peg of £3.8m at completion","Key management team (8 staff) to sign 24-month retention agreements"],"notes":"Seller obligations include a 12-month handover and 3-year non-compete. Warranties should include specific indemnities for the £23k bad debt and a cap at 50% of consideration. Completion via completion accounts with a working capital peg. Risk is low for the buyer as the price is anchored to earnings, not assets, and 40% is contingent on stopping the 'melting ice cube' effect."},{"name":"Balanced Approach","strategy":"A compromise structure that splits the difference between the earnings value (£5.2m) and the Net Asset Value (£11.4m) to acknowledge the strong balance sheet.","risk_to_buyer":"medium","suitable_when":"The buyer sees strategic value in the Sheffield facility and believes they can cross-sell to the existing 13 customers to halt the decline.","consideration":{"total_headline":8324944,"upfront_cash":4162472,"upfront_percent":50,"deferred":1664989,"earnout_maximum":2497483,"earnout_metric":"EBITDA Performance","earnout_period_months":24,"earnout_rationale":"Addresses 'Uncertain add-backs' (QoE Expert) regarding the management layer and 'Revenue decline' (Risk Expert). Earnout triggers if adjusted EBITDA exceeds £2.8m per annum.","retention_escrow":832494},"key_conditions":["No further dividend extraction between offer and completion","Satisfactory review of 2024 management accounts showing margin stability at 38%+","Change of control consents obtained for top 3 customers"],"notes":"Seller to provide 6-month full-time handover followed by 6-month consultancy. Standard warranty package with a 100% cap on upfront cash. Completion via locked-box mechanism to prevent further capital extraction. Risk is medium as the buyer is paying a premium over earnings for the asset base."},{"name":"Competitive Approach","strategy":"Aggressive offer anchored to the Net Asset Value (£11.4m) to meet seller expectations, but with significant deferred components to ensure the business doesn't collapse post-sale.","risk_to_buyer":"high","suitable_when":"A competitive bidding situation where the buyer intends to use the Sheffield facility as a hub for a larger group and values the 'clean' balance sheet.","consideration":{"total_headline":11427000,"upfront_cash":7427550,"upfront_percent":65,"deferred":1714050,"ea