y deal risk.","High customer concentration makes the business vulnerable to single-point failure.","The business is being 'harvested' by owners, with dividends depleting net assets."],"narrative":"Latest company Ltd is a high-quality operational shell that is losing its market relevance. While the balance sheet is strong, the P&L is in a state of controlled collapse. A successful deal must ignore the seller's anchor point of Net Asset Value and focus on the sustainable cash flow, which is significantly lower. The structure must use the top 5 customers as a 'security' for the deferred payments. If the seller insists on the £11.4m NAV, the deal should only proceed if the buyer has an immediate use for the Sheffield facility that does not depend on the existing, shrinking revenue stream."},"financial":{"expert":"financial","company_name":"Latest company Ltd","analysis_date":"2024-05-22","score":55,"confidence":"high","yearly_metrics":{"2020":{"revenue":28500000,"revenue_yoy_growth_percent":null,"cost_of_sales":17100000,"gross_profit":11400000,"gross_margin_percent":40,"administrative_expenses":4560000,"operating_profit":3420000,"operating_margin_percent":12,"depreciation_amortisation":1250000,"ebitda":4670000,"interest_payable":285000,"interest_coverage_ratio":12,"profit_before_tax":3135000,"corporation_tax":595650,"effective_tax_rate_percent":19,"net_profit":2539350,"net_margin_percent":8.91},"2021":{"revenue":26125000,"revenue_yoy_growth_percent":-8.33,"cost_of_sales":15675000,"gross_profit":10450000,"gross_margin_percent":40,"administrative_expenses":4186250,"operating_profit":3128750,"operating_margin_percent":11.98,"depreciation_amortisation":1181250,"ebitda":4310000,"interest_payable":261250,"interest_coverage_ratio":11.98,"profit_before_tax":2867500,"corporation_tax":0,"effective_tax_rate_percent":0,"net_profit":2328250,"net_margin_percent":8.91},"2022":{"revenue":23512500,"revenue_yoy_growth_percent":-10,"cost_of_sales":14107500,"gross_profit":9405000,"gross_ma