was zero, distorting net profit comparison","Detailed overhead breakdown missing for most years","Management accounts for late 2024 suggest further margin compression"]},"debt_service":{"latest_interest_coverage":12,"interest_coverage_trend":"stable","additional_debt_capacity_assessment":"High. Consistent 12x coverage and reducing long-term debt provide significant headroom for acquisition financing."},"key_findings":["Revenue has declined at a consistent 10% annual rate since 2021, indicating a shrinking market share or structural sector decline.","Gross and Operating margins are remarkably stable at 40% and 12% respectively, suggesting a highly disciplined variable cost model.","Staff costs are the primary overhead driver, representing approximately 42% of revenue, and have been scaled down in line with turnover.","The company maintains a very strong liquidity position with a current ratio of 2.0 and a quick ratio of 1.25.","Net assets are declining faster than retained profits suggest, indicating significant annual dividend distributions to shareholders.","Interest coverage is exceptionally robust at 12x, and the gearing ratio has improved to 26.3% as debt is amortised.","The 2024 management accounts suggest a potential dip in gross margin to 38%, which warrants immediate investigation."],"red_flags":["Persistent 4-year revenue contraction with a CAGR of -9.59%.","Significant customer concentration risk with the top 5 debtors representing 61.7% of the ledger.","Zero corporation tax charge in 2021 requires due diligence to ensure no underlying compliance issues or aggressive deferrals.","Declining net asset base suggests capital is being extracted rather than reinvested into growth."],"narrative":"From a financial performance perspective, Latest company Ltd presents a paradox of high operational discipline against a backdrop of terminal top-line decline. The company has successfully maintained a 40% gross margin and a 12% operating margin for five consecutive years, despite revenue falling from £28.5m to £19.0m. This suggests a highly flexible cost base where management has been able to shed staff and direct costs in perfect lockstep with falling sales. While this protects the bottom line in the short term, it indicates a business in 'harvest' mode rather than growth mode.\\n\\nEarnings quality is generally high, with net profit tracking operating profit closely, though the 2021 tax holiday and the consistent 8.91% net margin across varying scales suggest a level of accounting smoothing that requires deeper audit. The balance sheet is a position of strength; liquidity is excellent, and the company is under-leveraged with a gearing ratio of 26.3% and 12x interest coverage. This provides ample capacity for a buyer to introduce acquisition debt.\\n\\nHowever, the primary concern for any acquirer is the lack of organic growth. A 10% annual decline is difficult to reverse, and the high customer concentration (62% with five clients) makes the revenue stream fragile. The acquisition should only proceed if the buyer has a clear plan to integrate the company's efficient production capabilities into a growing sales channel, as the current trajectory leads to eventual irrelevance."}}	{"balanceSheet":{"id":322,"financialPeriodId":391,"targetCompanyId":78,"intangibleAssets":"516123","tangibleFixedAssets":"9516667","freeholdProperty":null,"leaseholdProperty":null,"plantMachinery":null,"fixturesFittings":null,"motorVehicles":null,"computerEquipment":null,"stockInventory":"2666667","tradeDebtors":"2986667","prepayments":null,"amountsOwedByDirectors":null,"amountsOwedByConnectedCompanies":null,"directorsCurrentAccount":null,"otherDebtors":null,"cashAtBank":"1012220","totalCurrentAssets":"6665554","tradeCreditors":null,"taxationSocialSecurity":null,"vatPayable":null,"corporationTaxDue":null,"bankLoansOverdraftCurrent":null,"hirePurchaseCurrent":null,"accruals":null,"amountsOwedToDirectors":null,"otherCreditors":null,"totalCurrentLiabilities":