ofitability, coinciding with a major capital expenditure programme into leasehold improvements and the introduction of bank debt. The 2025 results indicate a successful turnaround in top-line growth, with revenue returning to £1.06m. While the gross margin has structurally shifted lower (70% vs 81%) due to a change in the clinical labour mix (higher associate fees), the business has demonstrated improved operational leverage by containing administrative overheads during the recovery. The earnings quality is generally high, with EBITDA tracking the revenue recovery well. However, the buyer should be aware of the aggressive dividend policy; the current owners are extracting cash in excess of net earnings, which has led to a slight decline in the equity base. From an M&A perspective, the business is now right-sized with a modernised facility and a manageable gearing ratio of 27.4%. The primary risk for a buyer is the sustainability of the current revenue growth given the high marketing dependency and the permanent step-down in gross margin. Provided the 2025 recovery is maintained, the practice offers a stable platform with strong interest coverage (21.2x) and robust cash reserves of £306k."}}	{"balanceSheet":{"id":339,"financialPeriodId":411,"targetCompanyId":87,"intangibleAssets":"0","tangibleFixedAssets":"241144","freeholdProperty":null,"leaseholdProperty":null,"plantMachinery":null,"fixturesFittings":null,"motorVehicles":null,"computerEquipment":null,"stockInventory":null,"tradeDebtors":"6537","prepayments":null,"amountsOwedByDirectors":null,"amountsOwedByConnectedCompanies":null,"directorsCurrentAccount":null,"otherDebtors":null,"cashAtBank":"306012","totalCurrentAssets":"312549","tradeCreditors":null,"taxationSocialSecurity":null,"vatPayable":null,"corporationTaxDue":null,"bankLoansOverdraftCurrent":"78018","hirePurchaseCurrent":null,"accruals":null,"amountsOwedToDirectors":null,"otherCreditors":"88730","totalCurrentLiabilities":"166748","bankLoansLongTerm":"3452