xtraction vehicle for the director, evidenced by the £185,000 intercompany loan and dividends that exceed earnings. For a buyer, the primary risk is the razor-thin net margin (1.04%) and the total lack of liquidity. Any acquisition must be contingent on the repayment of intercompany balances to restore working capital and a significant earn-out to mitigate the extreme owner-dependency."},"valuation":{"expert":"valuation","company_name":"Goldwire Financial Solutions Limited","analysis_date":"2025-05-20","score":55,"confidence":"medium","ebitda_multiple_valuation":{"adjusted_ebitda_base":71204,"sector_multiple_range":{"low":1.5,"mid":2.25,"high":3},"selected_multiple":2,"multiple_justification":"A multiple of 2.0x is selected, which is below the sector midpoint. While revenue growth is strong (45% CAGR), the business suffers from extreme margin compression, critical owner dependency, and a high-risk liquidity profile. The low-margin 'pass-through' nature of the subcontractor model prevents a higher premium.","premium_factors_applied":["Strong revenue growth (45% CAGR)","High revenue per employee (£1.57M/head)","Niche positioning in commercial finance"],"discount_factors_applied":["Severe gross margin compression (33% to 13.8%)","Extreme owner dependency (single director)","Liquidity crisis (Quick Ratio 0.09)","High reliance on external subcontractors","Aggressive capital extraction (dividends > profit)"],"enterprise_value_range":{"conservative":106806,"base":142408,"optimistic":178010}},"ev_to_equity_bridge":{"enterprise_value_base":142408,"plus_cash":13131,"minus_long_term_debt":0,"minus_director_loans":6239,"minus_bad_debt_provision":0,"minus_working_capital_adjustment":40000,"other_adjustments":[{"item":"Intercompany Loan Risk Discount","amount":92500,"description":"50% haircut on £185,000 intercompany loan due to recoverability concerns and liquidity impact."}],"equity_value":{"conservative":73698,"base":109300,"optimistic":144902}},"asset_based_valuation":{"net_a