s and poses a major recovery risk.","Dividends consistently exceed net profit, indicating capital extraction rather than business building.","Net profit margin of 1.04% provides zero safety buffer for an acquirer.","Total dependency on a single director and a volatile subcontractor network."],"narrative":"Goldwire Financial Solutions Limited presents a significant valuation challenge. On a revenue basis, the company appears to be a high-growth success story. However, the M&A reality is a business with razor-thin margins and a hollowed-out balance sheet. The primary valuation methodology (EBITDA Multiple) yields a base equity value of approximately £110k, after adjusting for the cost of a replacement manager and the risk associated with the £185k intercompany loan. The massive gap between revenue-based expectations and earnings-based value suggests that a deal is only likely with a significant earn-out structure or if the buyer can dramatically improve margins by bringing subcontractor functions in-house. Without the intercompany loan being repaid or guaranteed, the business is on the verge of a liquidity crisis."},"deal_structure":{"expert":"deal_structure","company_name":"Goldwire Financial Solutions Limited","analysis_date":"2025-05-20","score":38,"confidence":"high","structures":[{"name":"Conservative","strategy":"Asset-backed protection with heavy performance weighting to mitigate liquidity and owner-dependency risks.","suitable_when":"High risk profile, extreme owner dependency, and critical liquidity concerns identified in due diligence.","consideration":{"total_headline":110000,"upfront_cash":27500,"upfront_percent":25,"deferred":27500,"deferred_schedule":"Paid in two equal installments at month 6 and month 12 post-completion, subject to no warranty claims.","earnout_maximum":55000,"earnout_metric":"Net Profit Margin Maintenance & Subcontractor Retention","earnout_period_months":24,"earnout_rationale":"Protects the buyer against the 1% net margin eroding furt