ng profit has declined in absolute terms for two consecutive years, falling from £637k to £444k.","The Telecoms segment remains the primary revenue driver, but the Panels division saw a sharp 31.6% decline in 2026.","Interest coverage has improved dramatically to 49.4x as bank debt is amortised, enhancing the balance sheet's capacity for new debt.","Directors' remuneration is highly volatile, with pension contributions fluctuating between £90k and £221k, suggesting potential for profit normalisation.","Liquidity is a major strength, with a current ratio of 2.29 and over £1.5m in working capital.","Earnings quality in 2026 is impacted by a £69k tax credit and bad debt recoveries, masking a deeper decline in underlying trading."],"red_flags":["Significant gross margin erosion (660bps) between 2024 and 2026.","Revenue decline in the most recent year, specifically within the Panels division.","Operating profit CAGR is negative (-6.23%) despite positive revenue growth over the full period.","Trade debtors increased by 38.6% in 2024, outpacing revenue growth and suggesting potential collection lag."],"narrative":"DNA exhibits a bifurcated financial profile that requires careful consideration. On one hand, the company maintains an exceptionally strong balance sheet with robust liquidity (Current Ratio 2.29) and a rapidly de-leveraging capital structure. The interest coverage ratio of 49.4x is exemplary, providing a clear runway for an acquirer to introduce acquisition debt without stressing the business. However, the P&L trends are more concerning. While the company achieved a 7.47% revenue CAGR, the most recent year (2026) shows a 9.2% contraction. More critically, gross margins have slipped from nearly 33% to 26%, suggesting that DNA is struggling to pass on inflationary pressures in direct labour and materials to its clients. Operating profit has followed this downward trajectory, declining from £637k in 2024 to £444k in 2026. The quality of earnings in the latest period is also artificially supported by a significant corporation tax credit and bad debt recoveries. A buyer should focus on whether the 2026 revenue dip is a temporary cyclical correction in the Panels segment or a structural loss of market share. Furthermore, the high volatility in directors' pension contributions suggests that 'owner-managed' expenses could be normalised to reveal higher underlying EBITDA. In summary, DNA is a financially stable, low-risk target from a solvency perspective, but one that currently faces operational headwinds and margin compression that must be addressed to justify a premium valuation."}}	{"balanceSheet":{"id":275,"financialPeriodId":331,"targetCompanyId":67,"intangibleAssets":null,"tangibleFixedAssets":null,"freeholdProperty":null,"leaseholdProperty":null,"plantMachinery":null,"fixturesFittings":null,"motorVehicles":null,"computerEquipment":null,"stockInventory":null,"tradeDebtors":null,"prepayments":null,"amountsOwedByDirectors":null,"amountsOwedByConnectedCompanies":null,"directorsCurrentAccount":null,"otherDebtors":"267","cashAtBank":null,"totalCurrentAssets":"267","tradeCreditors":null,"taxationSocialSecurity":null,"vatPayable":null,"corporationTaxDue":null,"bankLoansOverdraftCurrent":null,"hirePurchaseCurrent":null,"accruals":null,"amountsOwedToDirectors":null,"otherCreditors":"500000","totalCurrentLiabilities":"500000","bankLoansLongTerm":null,"hirePurchaseLongTerm":null,"deferredTaxation":null,"otherLongTermDebt":null,"totalLongTermLiabilities":"0","shareCapital":"267","retainedEarnings":"0","totalEquity":"267","debtorsList":null,"creditorsList":null,"fixedAssetsDetail":null,"sourceDocumentId":380,"createdAt":"2026-04-15T07:46:53.946Z","updatedAt":"2026-04-15T07:48:02.295Z"},"fixedAssets":null}	\N	2026-04-15 07:49:57.341077	2026-04-15 08:23:05.974	share_sale
