eak.","High reliance on 94-day creditor terms; any supplier tightening would impact the equity bridge.","Aging ERP and warehouse racking require immediate post-acquisition capital."],"narrative":"Test Company is a high-quality, low-risk acquisition target with a defensible market position evidenced by its 29.2% gross margin consistency. The valuation of £1.1M (Equity Value) reflects a healthy 2.75x multiple on adjusted earnings. While the balance sheet is exceptionally clean, the 'Quality of Earnings' adjustment is vital here; the buyer must normalize for the 2025 exceptional distribution costs to see the true earning power. The primary value-creation lever for an acquirer is operational: reversing the 4-year trend of payroll creep and modernizing the aging IT infrastructure. The business represents a stable platform for a trade buyer, though negotiations will likely hinge on the buyer's willingness to pay for the 'add-backs' versus the seller's recognition of the impending capex requirements."},"deal_structure":{"expert":"deal_structure","company_name":"Test Company","analysis_date":"2024-05-22","score":82,"confidence":"high","structures":[{"name":"Conservative","strategy":"Asset-backed upfront with heavy performance-contingent deferred payments to mitigate payroll inefficiency and capex risks.","suitable_when":"The buyer is concerned about the 'payroll creep' and the 2025 exceptional distribution costs being recurring rather than one-off.","consideration":{"total_headline":1100000,"upfront_cash":675000,"upfront_percent":61.4,"deferred":125000,"deferred_schedule":"Paid in two equal installments at month 12 and 24, subject to no warranty claims.","earnout_maximum":300000,"earnout_metric":"Adjusted EBITDA","earnout_period_months":24,"earnout_rationale":"Tied to achieving the 'Base Case' EBITDA of £364k. Protects buyer if the 2025 distribution costs recur or payroll costs cannot be reduced.","retention_escrow":100000,"escrow_release_conditions":"Released after 18 months following completion of the ERP and racking audit and any identified indemnity claims."},"seller_obligations":{"handover_period_months":12,"non_compete_months":36,"non_compete_scope":"Electrical wholesale and construction distribution within a 50-mile radius of current operations.","consultancy_arrangement":"Retain one director on a part-time consultancy basis for 12 months to manage supplier relationships."},"warranties_indemnities":{"specific_indemnities":["Specific indemnity for ERP system failure within first 6 months","Indemnity for any historical payroll tax underpayments related to the 2020-2024 headcount surge","Indemnity for stock obsolescence exceeding £25k"],"warranty_cap_percent":50,"warranty_period_months":24,"de_minimis":5000,"basket":15000},"completion_mechanism":{"type":"completion_accounts","working_capital_peg":518000,"rationale":"Given the high stock levels and 94-day creditor terms, a completion accounts mechanism ensures the buyer doesn't inherit a working capital deficit."},"effective_price":{"best_case":1100000,"expected_case":950000,"worst_case":675000}},{"name":"Balanced","strategy":"Standard market split with a focus on bridging the valuation gap through a 12-month earnout.","suitable_when":"Due diligence confirms the 2025 distribution costs are truly one-off and the seller agrees to a structured handover.","consideration":{"total_headline":1100000,"upfront_cash":825000,"upfront_percent":75,"deferred":100000,"deferred_schedule":"Single payment at month 12.","earnout_maximum":175000,"earnout_metric":"Gross Margin % and EBITDA","earnout_period_months":12,"earnout_rationale":"Ensures the 29.2% gross margin is maintained while the buyer implements payroll efficiencies.","retention_escrow":65000,"escrow_release_conditions":"Released upon successful implementation of the new ERP system or 12 months, whichever is sooner."},"seller_obligations":{"handover_period_months":6,"non_compete_months":24,"non_compete_scope":"Direct competition in the con