ow slight pressure in 2024 as admin expenses (3.3%) outpaced revenue growth (2.6%).","Strong earnings quality with net profit tracking operating profit closely and a consistent 19% effective tax rate.","Interest coverage has nearly doubled from 22.5x to 39.9x, driven by debt repayment and steady earnings.","Staff costs are the primary overhead driver, representing over 60% of administrative expenses.","Healthy cash generation evidenced by the increasing cash balance and consistent reduction in long-term debt."],"red_flags":["Administrative expenses have occasionally grown faster than revenue, suggesting a need for tighter overhead control as the business scales."],"narrative":"Test Company demonstrates the financial profile of a mature, well-managed electrical wholesale business. The most striking feature of the performance is the extreme consistency of the gross margin, which has remained at approximately 29.2% for five consecutive years. This suggests strong pricing power and effective procurement management in a sector often prone to commodity price volatility. Revenue growth is organic and steady, averaging 3.1% CAGR, which, while not aggressive, indicates a reliable and defensive income stream. From a profitability standpoint, the company maintains a 5% net margin with high earnings quality; there is no evidence of aggressive accounting or reliance on one-off gains. The balance sheet has strengthened significantly over the period, with long-term debt reducing from £125k to £65k, and interest coverage improving to nearly 40x. This provides a very high degree of 'headroom' for a buyer to introduce acquisition debt. The cost structure is largely variable (Cost of Sales at 71%), though staff costs are the significant fixed component. For an acquirer, the business represents a low-risk, 'steady-state' platform with robust cash flows and a clean balance sheet, though future value creation will likely depend on achieving operational synergies in the administrative cost base, which has shown signs of creeping upwards relative to top-line growth."}}	{"balanceSheet":{"id":42,"financialPeriodId":45,"targetCompanyId":14,"intangibleAssets":"0","tangibleFixedAssets":"195300","freeholdProperty":null,"leaseholdProperty":null,"plantMachinery":null,"fixturesFittings":null,"motorVehicles":null,"computerEquipment":null,"stockInventory":"512000","tradeDebtors":"438500","prepayments":null,"amountsOwedByDirectors":null,"amountsOwedByConnectedCompanies":null,"directorsCurrentAccount":null,"otherDebtors":null,"cashAtBank":"204200","totalCurrentAssets":"1154700","tradeCreditors":null,"taxationSocialSecurity":null,"vatPayable":null,"corporationTaxDue":null,"bankLoansOverdraftCurrent":null,"hirePurchaseCurrent":null,"accruals":null,"amountsOwedToDirectors":null,"otherCreditors":null,"totalCurrentLiabilities":"608400","bankLoansLongTerm":null,"hirePurchaseLongTerm":null,"deferredTaxation":null,"otherLongTermDebt":null,"totalLongTermLiabilities":"60000","shareCapital":"100","retainedEarnings":"681500","totalEquity":"681600","debtorsList":null,"creditorsList":null,"fixedAssetsDetail":null,"sourceDocumentId":69,"createdAt":"2026-03-19T00:50:40.230Z","updatedAt":"2026-03-19T00:50:40.230Z"},"fixedAssets":{"id":9,"targetCompanyId":14,"reportDate":"2024-01-31","totalGrossBookValue":"321800","totalAccumulatedDepreciation":"136616","totalNetBookValue":"185184","propertyGrossValue":"57000","propertyNetBookValue":"32000","plantMachineryGrossValue":"132000","plantMachineryNetBookValue":"74219","vehiclesGrossValue":"85000","vehiclesNetBookValue":"54958","itEquipmentGrossValue":"32700","itEquipmentNetBookValue":"13267","otherAssetsGrossValue":"15100","otherAssetsNetBookValue":"10740","refinanceableAssetsValue":"111115","fullyDepreciatedStillInUse":"0","assetItems":[{"description":"Warehouse Conveyor System","category":"Plant & Machinery","purchase_date":"2023-09-03","cost":38000,"accumulated_depreciation":5937,"net_book_value":32063,"depreciation_rate":12.5,"depre