tion_mechanism":{"type":"locked_box","working_capital_peg":1086752,"rationale":"Simplifies the closing process for the seller."},"effective_price":{"best_case":3000000,"expected_case":3000000,"worst_case":2700000}}],"recommended_structure":"Balanced","recommendation_rationale":"The Balanced structure is optimal because it addresses the valuation gap (sellers likely expect £3.5M+) by offering a solid upfront amount while using a small earnout to validate the premium 3.25x multiple. The business is high-quality and debt-free, so a heavy earnout (Conservative) might alienate the seller, but the customer concentration and tech-team reliance justify some contingent protection.","negotiation_priorities":["Verification of the £1.05M cash balance and its treatment as 'excess' vs 'working' capital.","Securing long-term contracts or 'key man' clauses for the 9-person tech team.","Confirming the 85% gross margin sustainability against potential wage inflation."],"deal_breaker_terms":["Loss of any of the Top 3 clients (Blackstone, M&G, Aberdeen) prior to completion.","Resignation of more than 2 members of the technical development team during due diligence.","Discovery of undisclosed director loans or intercompany liabilities."],"key_findings":["The business is exceptionally clean with no debt and high cash reserves.","Valuation is sensitive to the 3.25x multiple which is a premium for this scale.","Operational risk is concentrated in the tech team, not the owners.","Negative cash conversion cycle makes this an ideal 'buy and build' platform."],"narrative":"Team Test Co is a rare 'fortress' SME. With 85% margins and a negative cash conversion cycle, it is operationally elite. The primary challenge in structuring is the gap between the EBITDA-based Equity Value (£2.88M) and the seller's likely revenue-anchored expectations (£3.5M+). A Balanced structure offering ~70% upfront cash, supported by the company's own £1.05M cash pile, provides a compelling offer while protecting the b