"red_flags":["Moderate customer concentration risk: the top 5 debtors represent over 51% of the total sales ledger."],"narrative":"Aithon Solutions presents an exceptionally strong financial profile for acquisition. The company has demonstrated consistent organic revenue growth of 15% CAGR over the last four years, paired with a remarkably stable gross margin of 85%. This stability suggests significant pricing power and a well-controlled direct cost base. Profitability is not only high but is improving; net margins have expanded from 13.4% to 17.6%, indicating that the business is successfully leveraging its fixed overheads as it scales. \\n\\nFrom an earnings quality perspective, the performance is 'clean'. Operating profit translates predictably into net profit, with no evidence of exceptional items or aggressive accounting adjustments. The balance sheet is a particular area of strength; the company has transitioned to a zero-debt position while simultaneously building a cash reserve of over £1.05m. Liquidity is robust, with a current ratio of 4.64, providing a significant safety buffer. \\n\\nThe cost structure is dominated by staff costs, which is typical for the IT Services sector, but the business has managed to grow its headcount to 22 while maintaining high profitability per employee. The debt serviceability is peer-leading, with an interest coverage ratio of 288x, suggesting the company could easily support substantial acquisition debt if required. The only minor concern is a moderate level of customer concentration in the sales ledger, though the blue-chip nature of the debtors (e.g., Blackstone, Aberdeen Standard) mitigates the credit risk. Overall, Aithon is a high-performing, low-risk target with excellent financial momentum."}}	{"balanceSheet":{"id":287,"financialPeriodId":347,"targetCompanyId":70,"intangibleAssets":"295600","tangibleFixedAssets":"248900","freeholdProperty":null,"leaseholdProperty":null,"plantMachinery":null,"fixturesFittings":null,"mo