% organic growth rate driven by the high-margin (85%) software model.","Maintenance of blue-chip client relationships despite high concentration (51% in top 5)."],"sensitivity_factors":["Loss of any single top-5 debtor would impact EBITDA by approximately 10%.","Wage inflation for specialized ML/AI talent could compress the current 21.8% operating margin."],"upside_scenarios":["Utilization of the £1.05m cash 'war chest' for non-organic acquisition or rapid scaling.","Operational gearing improvements as revenue grows faster than the predominantly fixed cost base."],"downside_scenarios":["Key person dependency if the two directors exit without a sufficient handover of technical IP.","Technological obsolescence of the core AI platform if R&D investment does not keep pace with the sector."]},"key_findings":["Earnings are of exceptionally high quality with a clean audit trail and no evidence of aggressive accounting.","The business has successfully transitioned to a zero-debt position while maintaining high growth.","Adjusted EBITDA is higher than reported EBITDA primarily due to owner-directors taking salaries above SME market benchmarks.","The 85% gross margin is a significant indicator of pricing power and scalability."],"red_flags":["Customer concentration: 51% of revenue from 5 clients creates a 'cliff edge' risk for earnings sustainability.","Linear headcount growth: Staff costs are scaling with revenue, suggesting the model is not yet fully automated."],"narrative":"Aithon Solutions represents a high-quality acquisition target with 'clean' earnings and a robust balance sheet. The reported EBITDA of £519k is well-supported by cash flow and high-quality debtors. Our adjustments result in a Base Case Adjusted EBITDA of £542k, a 4.4% increase over reported figures. This is driven by normalizing director salaries, which are currently above market rates for a business of this size. We have applied prudent deductions for aging server infrastructure and a specific overdue