nagement.","Supplier credit (creditor days 52) remains available to fund the 130-day debtor cycle."],"sensitivity_factors":["Gross margin sensitivity to material inflation (600bps erosion already noted).","Impact of a single major debtor default (Top debtor is 50% of ledger in some periods)."],"upside_scenarios":["Implementing professional credit control to reduce debtor days from 130 to 90, freeing up significant cash.","Centralising procurement to recover the 6% gross margin lost since 2018."],"downside_scenarios":["Major housebuilder client insolvency leading to significant bad debt write-off.","Immediate requirement for £200k+ capital expenditure to replace aged plant and machinery."]},"key_findings":["Reported EBITDA is significantly overstated due to owner-directors taking minimal salaries in favor of dividends.","The business is highly operationally geared but faces a 'capex cliff' with its aging plant and machinery.","Working capital management is the primary risk, with MSL effectively acting as a bank for national housebuilders."],"red_flags":["Debtor days reaching 130 days suggests lack of leverage with major clients.","Plant and Machinery NBV is only 15% of cost, indicating imminent heavy reinvestment requirement.","Gross margin has compressed every year since 2018, falling from 40.7% to 34.6%."],"narrative":"MSL is a fundamentally profitable business, but its reported EBITDA of £365k is not a 'transferable' figure. The most significant adjustment is the requirement to normalize management pay; the current owners are underpaid by approximately £87k relative to the cost of hiring a replacement MD and FD. Furthermore, the business has likely under-invested in its asset base, with plant and machinery nearing the end of its useful life. While the 2022 revenue recovery was strong, the persistent erosion of gross margins and the extreme 130-day payment cycle from housebuilders create a high-risk profile. The adjusted EBITDA of £247k (Base Case) represents a more realistic starting point for valuation, accounting for the true operational costs and risks inherent in the specialist contracting sector."},"valuation":{"expert":"valuation","company_name":"MSL","analysis_date":"2023-10-27","score":75,"confidence":"high","ebitda_multiple_valuation":{"adjusted_ebitda_base":247534,"sector_multiple_range":{"low":1.5,"mid":2.25,"high":3},"selected_multiple":2.25,"multiple_justification":"A mid-range sector multiple is applied. While MSL shows strong historical net margins and a 2022 revenue recovery, the valuation is heavily constrained by its micro-cap scale (<£2M revenue), extreme customer concentration (top 5 > 90%), and an imminent capex cycle for aging plant assets.","premium_factors_applied":["Strong 2022 revenue growth (26.9%)","High operational gearing and net margins","Solid liquidity and freehold property ownership"],"discount_factors_applied":["Micro-cap scale (<£2M revenue)","Critical customer concentration (Top customer > 50%)","Aging plant and machinery (NBV 15% of cost)","High debtor days (130 days) indicating low leverage"],"enterprise_value_range":{"conservative":369897,"base":556951,"optimistic":790692}},"ev_to_equity_bridge":{"enterprise_value_base":556951,"plus_cash":187000,"minus_long_term_debt":176000,"minus_director_loans":0,"minus_bad_debt_provision":169626,"minus_working_capital_adjustment":0,"equity_value":{"conservative":211271,"base":398325,"optimistic":632066}},"asset_based_valuation":{"net_asset_value":519000,"property_adjustment":0,"bad_debt_adjustment":-169626,"adjusted_nav":349374,"nav_as_floor":true},"revenue_multiple_crosscheck":{"latest_revenue":1509696,"revenue_multiple_range":{"low":0.3,"high":0.5},"implied_ev_range":{"low":452908,"high":754848}},"valuation_summary":{"recommended_range":{"equity_value_low":350000,"equity_value_mid":400000,"equity_value_high":550000},"primary_methodology":"ebitda_multiple","cross_check_alignment":"strong"},"sensitivity":{"ebitda_plus_10pct":{"enterprise_value":612646,"equity_value":454020},"ebitda_minus_10pct":{"enterprise_value":501256,"equity_value":342630},"multiple_plus_half":{"enterprise_value":680718,"equity_value":522092},"multiple_minus_half":{"enterprise_value":433184,"equity_value":274558},"key_customer_loss_impact":"Loss of the top customer (50.6% of ledger) would likely render the business loss-making on an adjusted basis due to fixed overheads and debt service.","director_replacement_impact":"Replacing owners with market-rate management reduces EBITDA by £87,205, a 24% reduction from reported figures."},"seller_expectations":{"likely_seller_expectation_range":{"low":750000,"high":1200000},"seller_anchor_points":["Reported EBITDA of £365k (ignoring salary normalization)","High historical dividend payouts (£205k in 2022)","Emotional value of the freehold property acquisition"],"negotiation_gap_assessment":"Significant. Sellers will likely anchor on a 3x multiple of *reported* EBITDA (~£1.1M EV). The gap is driven by the £87k salary adjustment and the £170k bad debt provision which the seller will likely contest."},"key_findings":["Adjusted EBITDA is 32% lower than reported due to owner-director salary normalization.","The business is a net consumer of working capital with a 130-day debtor cycle.","Freehold property provides a solid valuation floor, but plant assets require urgent reinvestment.","Revenue growth is strong but margin compression (600bps) suggests declining pricing power."],"red_flags":["33% of the sales ledger is over 90 days overdue.","Extreme customer concentration (HHI Index 2950).","Plant and Machinery NBV is only 15.6% of cost, indicating a 'capex cliff'."],"narrative":"MSL is a high-margin specialist contractor that presents a classic SME valuation challenge: strong cash generation vs. high operational risk. While the reported EBITDA of £365k is attractive, it is inflated by under-market director salaries and deferred maintenance. After normalizing for a professional management structure and provisioning for a highly aged debtor book, the transferable EBITDA drops to £247k. The valuation is further tempered by the company's reliance on a handful of national housebuilders. A fair Equity Value sits around £400k, though a deal structure involving an earn-out or debt-recovery escrow will be essential to bridge the gap between the buyer's risk assessment and the seller's likely higher expectations."},"deal_structure":{"expert":"deal_structure","company_name":"MSL","analysis_date":"2023-10-27","score":55,"confidence":"high","structures":[{"name":"Conservative","strategy":"Maximum buyer protection through heavy deferment and risk-linked earnouts to mitigate extreme customer concentration and bad debt risks.","suitable_when":"The buyer is highly risk-averse and concerned about the 'capex cliff' and the 130-day debtor cycle.","consideration":{"total_headline":400000,"upfront_cash":160000,"upfront_percent":40,"deferred":80000,"deferred_schedule":"Paid in two equal installments of £40,000 at month 12 and month 24 post-completion.","earnout_maximum":160000,"earnout_metric":"Retention of Top 3 Customers and EBITDA Floor","earnout_period_months":24,"earnout_rationale":"Triggered by Customer Concentration (>20% single customer) and Owner Dependency. Identified by Risk and QoE experts.","retention_escrow":169626,"escrow_release_conditions":"Released pound-for-pound as the specific £169k of 90+ day aged debt identified at completion is collected."},"seller_obligations":{"handover_period_months":12,"non_compete_months":36,"non_compete_scope":"Specialist electrical and lighting contracting within the UK residential housebuilding sector.","consultancy_arrangement":"Directors to remain on part-time consultancy for months 7-12 to ensure relationship transfer to new MD."},"warranties_indemnities":{"specific_indemnities":["Full indemnity for any bad debt write-offs from the completion sales ledger exceeding the provision.","Indemnity for any undisclosed liabilities related to Ilke Homes insolvency.","Environmental indemnity related to the freehold property."],"warranty_cap_percent":50,"warranty_period_months":24,"de_minimis":2500,"basket":10000},"completion_mechanism":{"type":"completion_accounts","working_capital_peg":350000,"rationale":"Required due to the high volatility in debtor days and the need to verify the £169k aged debt at the exact point of transfer."},"effective_price":{"best_case":400000,"expected_case":320000,"worst_case":160000}},{"name":"Balanced","strategy":"A middle-ground approach using a mix of upfront cash and performance-based earnouts to bridge the valuation gap.","suitable_when":"Standard acquisition scenario where the seller accepts the need to prove the recoverability of debtors and customer stickiness.","consideration":{"total_headline":475000,"upfront_cash":285000,"upfront_percent":60,"deferred":95000,"deferred_schedule":"Paid 12 months post-completion.","earnout_maximum":95000,"earnout_metric":"Gross Margin Maintenance and Top Customer Retention","earnout_period_months":12,"earnout_rationale":"Triggered by Customer Concentration (Top customer >50%) and Margin Erosion (600bps decline). Identified by Risk and QoE experts.","retention_escrow":85000,"escrow_release_conditions":"Released upon 50% recovery of the 90+ day debt ledger within 6 months."},"seller_obligations":{"handover_period_months":6,"non_compete_months":24,"non_compete_scope":"Direct competition in the lighting installation sector for national housebuilders.","consultancy_arrangement":"Ad-hoc consultancy for 6 months following the initial handover."},"warranties_indemnities":{"specific_indemnities":["Specific indemnity for the recovery of the top customer's outstanding balance.","Indemnity for any tax liabilities arising from historical dividend treatments."],"warranty_cap_percent":100,"warranty_period_months":18,"de_minimis":5000,"basket":15000},"completion_mechanism":{"type":"completion_accounts","working_capital_peg":350801,"rationale":"Aligns with the 2022 NWC to ensure the business is transferred with sufficient liquidity to fund the long debtor cycle."},"effective_price":{"best_case":475000,"expected_case":425000,"worst_case":285000}},{"name":"Competitive","strategy":"Aggressive upfront offer to secure the deal in a competitive process, relying on warranties rather than earnouts for protection.","suitable_when":"Multiple bidders are present and the buyer has high confidence in the sector's resilience.","consideration":{"total_headline":550000,"upfront_cash":440000,"upfront_percent":80,"deferred":110000,"deferred_schedule":"Unconditional payment 12 months post-completion.","earnout_maximum":0,"earnout_metric":"None","earnout_period_months":0,"earnout_rationale":"No earnout included to remain competitive, despite triggers, shifting risk to warranties and the deferred payment set-off rights.","retention_escrow":50000,"escrow_release_conditions":"General retention for warranty claims, released after 12 months."},"seller_obligations":{"handover_period_months":3,"non_compete_months":24,"non_compete_scope":"Restricted from soliciting top 5 customers.","consultancy_arrangement":"None."},"warranties_indemnities":{"specific_indemnities":["Indemnity for bad debts exceeding 5% of the total ledger."],"warranty_cap_percent":100,"warranty_period_months":12,"de_minimis":10000,"basket":25000},"completion_mechanism":{"type":"locked_box","working_capital_peg":null,"rationale":"Provides price certainty to the seller, which is a competitive advantage in negotiations."},"effective_price":{"best_case":550000,"expected_case":525000,"worst_case":440000}}],"recommended_structure":"Conservative","recommendation_rationale":"The combination of extreme customer concentration (50% with one client), a 130-day debtor cycle, and a £169k aged debt issue makes a high-upfront deal reckless. The Conservative structure protects the buyer's capital by linking 60% of the value to the actual recovery of cash and the retention of the key customer base.","negotiation_priorities":["Verification of the £169k aged debt recoverability.","Securing a long-term commitment or contract renewal with Exterior Lighting Solutions (UK) Ltd.","Agreement on the 'Market Rate' salary adjustment for the incoming management team.","Establishing a clear Capex plan for the aging plant and machinery."],"deal_breaker_terms":["Refusal of a pound-for-pound escrow for debts over 90 days.","Inability to meet with the top customer during due diligence.","Discovery of significant bad debt write-offs involving Ilke Homes."],"key_findings":["The business is highly profitable but has a fragile risk profile due to customer concentration.","Reported EBITDA is inflated by approximately £87k due to low director salaries.","The 'Capex Cliff' (Plant NBV at 15% of cost) requires a price reduction or a structured holdback.","The 130-day debtor cycle effectively makes the buyer a lender to national housebuilders."],"narrative":"MSL presents a classic 'high-yield, high-risk' profile. While the margins are excellent, the operational dependencies are severe. A successful deal must bridge the gap between the seller's likely £1M+ expectation and the £400k-£500k realistic valuation. This is best achieved through a structure that pays for performance and cash recovery rather than historical accounting profit. The Conservative structure is recommended because it addresses the 'Bad Debt' and 'Customer Concentration' triggers identified by all experts, ensuring the buyer does not overpay for 'paper' profits that may never convert to cash."},"financial":{"expert":"financial","company_name":"MSL","analysis_date":"2023-10-27","score":78,"confidence":"high","yearly_metrics":{"2018":{"revenue":1285084,"revenue_yoy_growth_percent":null,"cost_of_sales":761525,"gross_profit":523559,"gross_margin_percent":40.74,"administrative_expenses":186609,"operating_profit":336973,"operating_margin_percent":26.22,"depreciation_amortisation":22926,"ebitda":359899,"interest_payable":1190,"interest_coverage_ratio":283.17,"profit_before_tax":335980,"corporation_tax":63933,"effective_tax_rate_percent":19.03,"net_profit":272047,"net_margin_percent":21.17},"2019":{"revenue":1419022,"revenue_yoy_growth_percent":10.42,"cost_of_sales":879388,"gross_profit":539634,"gross_margin_percent":38.03,"administrative_expenses":182936,"operating_profit":356698,"operating_margin_percent":25.14,"depreciation_amortisation":32040,"ebitda":388738,"interest_payable":1989,"interest_coverage_ratio":179.34,"profit_before_tax":354713,"corporation_tax":68211,"effective_tax_rate_percent":19.23,"net_profit":286502,"net_margin_percent":20.19},"2020":{"revenue":1280352,"revenue_yoy_growth_percent":-9.77,"cost_of_sales":805324,"gross_profit":475028,"gross_margin_percent":37.1,"administrative_expenses":179730,"operating_profit":323905,"operating_margin_percent":25.3,"depreciation_amortisation":27643,"ebitda":351548,"interest_payable":4633,"interest_coverage_ratio":69.91,"profit_before_tax":319498,"corporation_tax":61931,"effective_tax_rate_percent":19.38,"net_profit":257567,"net_margin_percent":20.12},"2021":{"revenue":1189472,"revenue_yoy_growth_percent":-7.1,"cost_of_sales":795745,"gross_profit":393727,"gross_margin_percent":33.1,"administrative_expenses":162648,"operating_profit":244400,"operating_margin_percent":20.55,"depreciation_amortisation":24509,"ebitda":268909,"interest_payable":9061,"interest_coverage_ratio":26.97,"profit_before_tax":235366,"corporation_tax":46270,"effective_tax_rate_percent":19.66,"net_profit":189096,"net_margin_percent":15.9},"2022":{"revenue":1509696,"revenue_yoy_growth_percent":26.92,"cost_of_sales":987487,"gross_profit":522209,"gross_margin_percent":34.59,"administrative_expenses":176575,"operating_profit":345634,"operating_margin_percent":22.89,"depreciation_amortisation":20131,"ebitda":365765,"interest_payable":9575,"interest_coverage_ratio":36.1,"profit_before_tax":336059,"corporation_tax":65234,"effective_tax_rate_percent":19.41,"net_profit":270825,"net_margin_percent":17.94}},"cagr":{"revenue_cagr_percent":4.11,"gross_profit_cagr_percent":-0.06,"operating_profit_cagr_percent":0.64,"period_years":4},"cost_structure":{"cost_of_sales_percent_revenue":65.41,"overheads_percent_revenue":11.7,"staff_costs_percent_revenue":3.83,"director_costs_percent_revenue":1.84,"top_5_overheads":[{"category":"Depreciation","value":20131,"percent_of_overheads":11.4},{"category":"Motor Expenses","value":16430,"percent_of_overheads":9.31},{"category":"Professional Fees","value":11236,"percent_of_overheads":6.36},{"category":"Telecommunications","value":7694,"percent_of_overheads":4.36},{"category":"Insurance","value":6170,"percent_of_overheads":3.49}],"cost_base_classification":"predominantly_variable"},"earnings_quality":{"net_profit_tracks_operating_profit":true,"exceptional_items_identified":["Government grants receivable: 10000 (2020)","Other operating income: 28607 (2020)","Other operating income: 13321 (2021)"],"tax_rate_consistent":true,"ebitda_latest":365765,"ebitda_trend":"growing","limitations":["Amortisation not separately disclosed from depreciation in summary P&L"]},"debt_service":{"latest_interest_coverage":36.1,"interest_coverage_trend":"deteriorating","additional_debt_capacity_assessment":"Strong. Despite the decline from 283x to 36x, the coverage remains well above banking covenants, supported by a low gearing ratio of 33.9%."},"key_findings":["Revenue recovered strongly in 2022 with 26.9% growth after two years of pandemic-related decline.","Gross margins have compressed from 40.7% (2018) to 34.6% (2022), indicating significant inflationary pressure on materials.","Operating efficiency is high; administrative expenses as a % of revenue fell from 14.5% to 11.7% over the period.","The company maintains a very high dividend payout ratio, often exceeding 75% of net profit, which limits internal capital reinvestment.","Cash generation is robust, with cash at bank increasing from £89k in 2018 to £187k in 2022 despite high dividends.","The balance sheet was significantly altered in 2020 by a £256k freehold property acquisition funded by new bank debt.","Customer concentration is a major risk, with national housebuilders dominating the sales ledger and extending payment cycles to 130 days."],"red_flags":["Significant gross margin erosion of 600bps since 2018.","High customer concentration: Top 5 debtors represent over 40% of the ledger.","Deteriorating debtor days, reaching 129.5 days in recent reports, suggesting poor collection leverage against large contractors.","High dividend dependency may necessitate a change in capital allocation post-acquisition."],"narrative":"MSL exhibits the financial profile of a mature, highly profitable specialist contractor within the construction sector. The company has demonstrated resilience, maintaining double-digit net margins (averaging 19%) throughout the 2018-2022 period, including the COVID-19 downturn. The 2022 recovery was particularly strong, with revenue reaching a five-year high of £1.51m. However, this growth has come at the cost of margin compression; gross margins have trended downwards from 40.7% to 34.6%, likely due to the inability to fully pass on material price increases to fixed-price contracts with national housebuilders.\\n\\nFrom an earnings quality perspective, the results are clean. Operating profit closely tracks net profit, and the reliance on government grants during the pandemic was modest. The cost structure is lean, with administrative overheads well-controlled and showing positive operational gearing during the 2022 revenue surge. The primary financial risk lies in the working capital cycle. Debtor days are exceptionally high (130 days), and the sales ledger is heavily concentrated among a few large residential developers. This creates a 'squeeze' where MSL must fund its variable cost base (65% of revenue) while waiting over four months for payment.\\n\\nThe balance sheet is solid, underpinned by freehold property and a manageable gearing ratio of 33.9%. While interest coverage has declined due to the debt taken on for the property purchase, a ratio of 36x remains extremely safe. For an acquirer, the business offers stable, high-margin earnings, but success will depend on managing the working capital requirement and addressing the downward trend in gross margins through better procurement or contract indexing."}}	{"balanceSheet":{"id":257,"financialPeriodId":307,"targetCompanyId":60,"intangibleAssets":null,"tangibleFixedAssets":"287495","freeholdProperty":"246696","leaseholdProperty":null,"plantMachinery":"40799","fixturesFittings":null,"motorVehicles":null,"computerEquipment":null,"stockInventory":"70027","tradeDebtors":"384404","prepayments":null,"amountsOwedByDirectors":null,"amountsOwedByConnectedCompanies":null,"directorsCurrentAccount":null,"otherDebtors":"7716","cashAtBank":"187563","totalCurrentAssets":"649710","tradeCreditors":"142923","taxationSocialSecurity":"63755","vatPayable":null,"corporationTaxDue":"67758","bankLoansOverdraftCurrent":"5964","hirePurchaseCurrent":null,"accruals":null,"amountsOwedToDirectors":null,"otherCreditors":"18509","totalCurrentLiabilities":"298909","bankLoansLongTerm":"154239","hirePurchaseLongTerm":null,"deferredTaxation":"7196","otherLongTermDebt":"0","totalLongTermLiabilities":"161435","shareCapital":"100","retainedEarnings":"476761","totalEquity":"476861","debtorsList":null,"creditorsList":null,"fixedAssetsDetail":null,"sourceDocumentId":341,"createdAt":"2026-04-05T17:26:53.421Z","updatedAt":"2026-04-05T17:26:53.421Z"},"fixedAssets":null}	\N	2026-04-05 17:33:42.989841	2026-04-15 19:47:22.208	share_sale
