improvements occurred in 2023 (£294k), but the lack of a detailed asset register prevents a full NBV/Cost freshness analysis. Current assets are primarily tangible fixed assets and cash."},"people_capability":{"rag":"AMBER","score":45,"headcount":null,"revenue_per_employee":null,"payroll_to_revenue_percent":12.2,"director_cost_percent_of_payroll":8.9,"explanation":"Director remuneration is low at £11,520, suggesting owner-dependency may be masked by dividend extractions. Staff costs as a % of revenue are low for the sector, but headcount data is missing to calculate productivity."}},"overall_score":56,"recommendation":"PROCEED_WITH_CAUTION","recommendation_justification":"The company is financially stable with strong cash reserves and low debt, but it is currently experiencing significant margin compression and scale volatility. The lack of sales ledger and staff headcount data prevents a full risk assessment of the operational core.","key_strengths":["Strong liquidity position with £306,012 in cash and a healthy current ratio of 1.9.","Low financial leverage with a gearing ratio that has improved to 27.4%.","Successful revenue recovery in 2025, returning to over £1m in turnover."],"key_concerns":["Significant net margin erosion, falling from 36.7% to 15.0% over the five-year period.","Aggressive dividend policy where payouts consistently exceed annual net profits, depleting the capital base.","High dependency on associates/subcontractors as evidenced by the sharp increase in cost of sales in 2025."],"questions_for_seller":["What caused the 18% revenue drop in 2024 and the subsequent 33% surge in 2025?","Can you provide a breakdown of the patient base between NHS and private contracts?","Why have dividend payments consistently exceeded net profit in recent years?","What is the current clinical headcount and the contractual status of the associates driving the 2025 cost increase?"],"comparable_context":"A net margin of 15% is slightly below the 20-25% typical for high-performing private dental practices, likely due to the high associate cost model. The cash-rich balance sheet is superior to many debt-heavy dental groups.","executive_summary":"Dental Surgery 70171 is recommended for 'Proceed with Caution'. The business demonstrates strong financial resilience, characterised by a robust cash position of £306,012 and a healthy current ratio of 1.9. It has successfully navigated a volatile period, recovering revenue to £1.06m in 2025. However, the primary concern is a clear trend of margin contraction; net margins have halved since 2021, and gross margins were impacted in 2025 by a 107% increase in associate-related costs. Furthermore, the current owners are extracting capital via dividends at a rate faster than profit generation, leading to a gradual erosion of net assets. The absence of sales ledger and headcount data leaves significant blind spots regarding patient concentration and staff productivity. Further investigation should focus on the sustainability of the current associate cost structure and the split between private and NHS income."}	\N	\N	\N	9685	{"promptTokenCount":30792,"candidatesTokenCount":1583,"totalTokenCount":32375}	59	{data_quality}	2026-04-24 22:22:24.371578	2026-04-24 22:22:34.103
