pany's 40% gross margin is superior to the typical 25-30% seen in IT services/manufacturing hybrids, but the revenue CAGR of -9.6% significantly underperforms a sector usually seeing 5-8% growth.","executive_summary":"Brand New Company presents a paradox of high operational efficiency and financial stability set against a backdrop of terminal-looking revenue decline. The business has successfully maintained 40% gross margins and ~9% net margins despite turnover falling from 28.5m to 19m over four years. This suggests a very disciplined management team capable of scaling costs (headcount reduced from 142 to 122) in line with activity. Balance sheet health is a core strength, with a current ratio of 2.0 and a manageable gearing of 26%. However, the 'Cash Reality' is less positive; cash at bank is declining as the owners appear to be extracting value faster than the business is growing. Furthermore, the sales ledger reveals a high dependency on a small cluster of clients. This is a 'Proceed with Caution' because while the business is not in immediate distress, the buyer must determine if the revenue slide can be arrested or if they are simply buying a high-quality melting ice cube."}	\N	\N	\N	10698	{"promptTokenCount":37988,"candidatesTokenCount":1654,"totalTokenCount":39642}	34	{data_quality}	2026-04-20 18:42:07.994209	2026-04-20 18:42:18.739
