ation based on adjusted earnings rather than the £5.4m intercompany debt anchor.","consideration":{"total_headline":525000,"upfront_cash":262500,"upfront_percent":50,"deferred":131250,"earnout_maximum":131250,"earnout_metric":"Revenue Retention","earnout_period_months":24,"earnout_rationale":"Trigger 2 (Revenue stagnation risk): Due to the 81% cut in advertising, there is a high risk of revenue decay. This earnout protects the buyer if the £5.3m revenue base falls below a £5m floor post-acquisition.","retention_escrow":50000},"key_conditions":["Formalization of the lease agreement for the property at market rates.","Evidence of contractor/agency labor contracts to mitigate the 2-person headcount risk.","Director loan accounts (£156k) to be cleared at completion."],"notes":"6-month handover period followed by 12 months of consultancy. Standard warranty package with a 100% cap on upfront cash. Locked-box mechanism based on the 2024 accounts, provided no leakage occurs via intercompany transfers. Risk is medium as the buyer takes on more upfront cost while the 'Capex Cliff' remains a looming operational requirement."},{"name":"Competitive Approach","strategy":"Maximizing upfront cash to bridge the gap with seller expectations, relying on strong legal indemnities rather than contingent payments.","risk_to_buyer":"high","suitable_when":"A competitive bidding environment where the buyer values the £5.3m revenue stream and the negative cash conversion cycle highly.","consideration":{"total_headline":600000,"upfront_cash":450000,"upfront_percent":75,"deferred":150000,"earnout_maximum":0,"earnout_metric":"N/A","earnout_period_months":0,"earnout_rationale":"No earnout included to increase offer competitiveness; risk is instead managed through a lower headline price relative to seller expectations and strict completion adjustments.","retention_escrow":442000},"key_conditions":["Full retention of the HMRC settlement amount (£442k) until cash is received by the company.","Person