st revenue growth?"],"comparable_context":"In the UK electrical wholesale sector, a 29% gross margin is upper-quartile, typically indicating strong local brand loyalty or a specialised product mix. The 5% net margin is standard for the industry, where high logistics and staff costs are common.","executive_summary":"Test Company is a highly stable electrical wholesale business that warrants immediate further investigation. The company has demonstrated consistent revenue growth from 2.85m to 3.22m over the last five years while maintaining remarkably steady gross margins of 29.2%. Financially, the business is in excellent health; it is lowly geared (9.8%), highly liquid (Current Ratio 1.87), and generates cash in line with its reported profits. The sales ledger is high quality, with minimal bad debt risk and a diversified customer base. While growth is steady rather than aggressive, the lack of 'red flags' in the earnings, cash, or balance sheet dimensions makes this a low-risk platform acquisition. Key areas for due diligence should focus on the scalability of the current warehouse operations and the age of the internal ERP systems."}	\N	\N	\N	10339	{"promptTokenCount":38226,"candidatesTokenCount":1618,"totalTokenCount":39844}	1	{data_quality}	2026-03-19 00:51:34.554354	2026-03-19 00:51:44.947
