actions; warranty cap at 25% of consideration for general claims. Completion mechanism: Completion accounts. Risk to buyer is high due to extreme valuation disconnect and the risk that the 2026 recovery is not sustainable without the owners' personal networks."}],"recommended_structure":"Conservative Approach","recommendation_rationale":"The business is currently loss-making on an adjusted basis and has experienced a 48% revenue collapse. Paying anything above the Net Asset Value (£63.7k) is speculative. The Conservative Approach protects the buyer by only paying for tangible assets upfront and tying all 'goodwill' to the actual realization of the 2026 recovery and the successful handover of owner relationships.","negotiation_priorities":["Verification of the 98% Gross Margin reported in 2026 trial balance","Securing a long-term commitment from the Operations Manager","Ensuring the £36.9k Director Loan is repaid to the company at completion","Bridging the massive gap between the £63k NAV and the £250k+ seller expectation"],"deal_breaker_terms":["Refusal of the owners to provide a minimum 12-month handover","Discovery that 2026 margins are inflated by misallocating staff costs to overheads","Further dividend extraction prior to completion"],"key_findings":["The business is in a turnaround phase following a disastrous 2025.","Valuation is currently anchored to assets, not earnings, due to negative adjusted EBITDA.","Extreme key person risk exists with both 50% shareholders exiting simultaneously.","Accounting anomalies in 2026 data suggest significant due diligence is required before committing to a price."],"narrative":"Hayward Miller is a high-risk acquisition. The 2025 financial year showed a business in freefall, with revenue halving and margins collapsing. While 2026 data suggests a miraculous recovery, the lack of forensic detail makes this recovery suspect. The owners have been extracting capital (dividends and pensions) at a rate that exceeds the company's earnings, eroding the capital base. Any deal must be structured to ensure the buyer is not overpaying for a 'lifestyle' business that may not survive the exit of its founders. The recommended Conservative Approach focuses on capital preservation, paying only for the net assets upfront and requiring the sellers to 'earn' the rest of the valuation by proving the business is stable and the 2026 margins are legitimate."}	\N	32	high	17605	{"promptTokenCount":7214,"candidatesTokenCount":1858,"totalTokenCount":10457}	42	{valuation,risk,operational,qoe}	2026-04-25 12:14:37.121201	2026-04-25 12:16:21.509
