sitive operational gearing during the 2022 revenue surge. The primary financial risk lies in the working capital cycle. Debtor days are exceptionally high (130 days), and the sales ledger is heavily concentrated among a few large residential developers. This creates a 'squeeze' where MSL must fund its variable cost base (65% of revenue) while waiting over four months for payment.\\n\\nThe balance sheet is solid, underpinned by freehold property and a manageable gearing ratio of 33.9%. While interest coverage has declined due to the debt taken on for the property purchase, a ratio of 36x remains extremely safe. For an acquirer, the business offers stable, high-margin earnings, but success will depend on managing the working capital requirement and addressing the downward trend in gross margins through better procurement or contract indexing."}	\N	78	high	14296	{"promptTokenCount":41389,"candidatesTokenCount":2767,"totalTokenCount":44156}	11	\N	2026-04-05 17:30:14.553473	2026-04-05 17:30:29.442
