cture\n●\nFounder-led business\n●\n●\n●\nOwners likely responsible for:\n○\nSupplier relationships\n○\nStrategy\n○\nMarketing/social media\nStore teams manage day-to-day operations\nNo clear second-tier management layer\n●\nKey risk:\n○\nFounder dependency - happy to stay on for the foreseeable to make sure the\nbusiness runs how it should.\nSystems and Tech Stack\n●\nLikely basic systems:\n○\nPOS\n●\n●\n○\nInventory management\nE-commerce exists but underdeveloped\nNo clear evidence of:\n○\nCRM\n○\n●\nOpportunity:\n○\n○\nAdvanced analytics\nDigital transformation\nE-commerce scaling\nProperty\n●\nThree leased stores:\n○\n○\n○\nLeeds (~7,000 sqft flagship)\nBirmingham (~3,400 sqft)\nCrewe (~3,000 sqft)\n●\nFeatures:\n○\n○\nCustomer parking\nExperiential retail (e.g. test tracks)\n●\nFixed cost base from leases\n●\nKey risks:\n○\nLease terms\n○\nRent increases\nOwner Overview\n●\n●\n●\n●\n●\nTwo equal shareholders (founders)\nBuilt business organically\nStrong operational involvement\nSelling to pursue “new chapter”\nLikely key drivers of:\n○\nBrand\n○\nCulture\n○\nGrowth\n●\nRisk:\n○\nBusiness may rely on them\nSWOT Analysis\nStrengths\n●\n●\n●\n●\nStrong brand reputation (3,000+ reviews)\nPremium positioning\nOrganic customer acquisition (low CAC)\nHigh-quality in-store experience\n●\nStrong recent financial turnaround\nWeaknesses\n●\n●\n●\n●\n●\nFounder dependency\nLimited management depth\nBasic systems/infrastructure\nWorking capital constraints\nOnly one year of strong profitability\nOpportunities\n●\n●\n●\n●\n●\nE-commerce expansion\nNew store expansion\nBroader product range\nMonetising social audience\nOperational improvements\nThreats\n●\n●\n●\n●\nSupplier dependency\nMargin sustainability risk\nRetail cost pressures (rent, wages)\nOnline competition\nEconomic sensitivity	2026-04-24 21:47:46.983716
